hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of ask Evan today  maintain a question from Virginia who's  one of my newsletter readers so she  wrote in saying she's 48 years old  single mother her her husband or  ex-husband I guess is not given any kind  of child support she hasn't had her  degree at she's studying part-time but  she wants to be able to follow her dream  and do something that she's really  passionate about and wanted my advice on  how to get going so it's a great  question I'm very sorry here but  situation hopefully that resolves itself  and now you're able to move on to a much  better life and and you know build  something that you can build around your  passion so my advice for you and this is  something that's asked a lot by a lot of  my readers is how do I find my passion  how do I build a business around and and  have the confidence to take that leap  what i would do to get started is make a  list of all the things that you are  really excited about and passionate  about things that you would do in your  part time spare time I know you may not  have a lot of your single mom when  you're studying and you have a job too  but what do you like to do it in your in  your part time and try to marry that  with what can you do to help people if  you're looking at starting the business  and being successful you have to be able  to provide a product or service that  provides a lot of value to other people  right they're going to be the ones  paying you so you're you may really love  playing computer games all day long but  if you're not adding tangible value to  other people then you're not going to be  able to really build successful business  off of it so that would be step number  one I then also look at what are some  frustrations that you solve in your own  life that maybe other people could could  have that help as well so through your  you know of course if your life had a  lot of experience you probably had a lot  of ups and downs through those down  times what are some of the biggest most  painful problems that you had to go  through and how can you potentially help  other people solve those problems the  bigger the pain is the more painful it  is for somebody the bigger the  frustration the more they're going to  want to pay you to help them solve it so  that's a key with any business if you  work if you're targeting the pain  a problem or frustration of somebody  it's going to be easier to build a  business off of it so we're starting  with something that we're really  passionate about with something or  something that there's a there's a pain  involved and we're starting with  something that we feel we can help other  people a lot of entrepreneurs make the  mistake of just trying to start a  business to make money and it's the  wrong way to go about it because if you  look at the most successful famous  entrepreneurs look at anybody who got  started they rarely started because they  wanted to make a lot of money it's  because they had a strong passion for  what they were doing they wanted to  change the way things were done in their  industry or they want to have a  meaningful impact on the people that  they were connecting with that's what  make them get started and that's what  made them keep going through all the  hard times and certainly business isn't  easy it can be very rewarding can be a  lot of fun it can be you know bringing a  lot of money if you stick with it but  there's a lot of hard times to get a  company off the ground and you're only  going to do it if you're really  passionate about what you're doing so I  try to make that list of ideas once  you've narrowed it down to see the top  three to five ideas I try to commit to  doing some more research on it so I  commit to doing at least an hour of  research on the internet for each idea  and also commit to going to the  bookstore or local library to do more  research on the idea now you can  probably find everything you need on the  internet so why would you go to a  bookstore library the reason is actually  getting out of your house going and  making that trip and get in a babysitter  or whatever you need to do to go there  commits you two doing a little bit on  that business and if you're not willing  to commit to going to do what trip to  the bookstore you're probably not going  to be able to make that business a  success right that's a that's a pretty  minimal equipment and you have to take  some seriously big commitments to make  that business take off so if there's  some ideas on there that you don't want  to go and make that trip for you can  probably scratch them off the list then  I look at which idea is that you just do  the bare minimum along and which ones  that you actually go out and really  spend a lot of time trying to figure out  so if the you know the assignment is  into one hour of internet research in  one hour at a bookstore which ideas did  you actually go and just do an hour on  and which idea is that you go way above  and beyond you kind of got lost in it  because you were so excited and  passionate about  I got so many new ideas from it and you  just poured your heart into it that's  the one that you want to really focus on  to build your business and the ones  we're just doing the bare minimum again  if you're an entrepreneur and you're  just doing the bare minimum you're not  going to have success you have to go way  above and beyond especially to launch a  new business so the one that you're  really focused on and you spent all that  extra time on that's probably the one  where you would want to start to to  build your company around from there  it's just starting to talk to customers  getting their feedback trying to build a  service that can help solve the problems  and invest the cash flow that you have  coming in and to continue to grow your  business but that's how it would start  up how to find my passion how to start a  business around that's something I'm  really excited about so hopefully that  helps again with your situation I hope  this can be a new opportunity for you to  discover yourself and live the best life  possible for yourself for those of you  watching if you liked the video please  give it a thumbs up it makes me want to  do more of these for you and if you have  a question about finding your passion or  about your business feel free to leave  in the comments below I always read  those we've how to respond to as many as  I can so thank you and we'll see you on  the next episode  you
 

